IMPORT prelude

-- Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts in months ("not resolved within 3 months of making the complaint",
-- s 5(2)(c); "more than 12 months after the provision of the health service was completed", s 8(1); "not ... more than
-- 12 months after the undertaking", s 39(2); "6 months following the receipt of the complaint", s 31(5)), in weeks
-- ("for up to 12 weeks", s 90(1)), in plain days ("within 28 days after the later of", s 101(2)) and in business days
-- (ss 15(2), 35(2), 41(2), 61(1), 65(4)(d); those are asked as counts, since public holidays are not in the Act).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Health
-- Complaints Act 2016, Version No. 011 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Health Complaints Act 2016`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- A number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month a number of months later (n positive) or earlier (n negative); where that month is shorter,
-- its last day (30 November 2026 plus 3 months is 28 February 2027; fork F2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months on from` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS `the date` n `months on from` `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months before` `the start` MEANS `the date` (0 MINUS n) `months on from` `the start`
